WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:02.790
INTRO:
10 years ago, Supercell was just about to

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:03.930
release Clash of Clans.

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:08.549
They didn’t know it at the time, but Clash
of Clans would become one of the most popular

00:00:08.549 --> 00:00:10.519
mobile games of all time.

00:00:10.519 --> 00:00:15.069
They would follow up Clash of Clans with Boom
Beach, Clash Royale, and Brawl Stars.

00:00:15.069 --> 00:00:19.720
And before you knew it, Supercell became one
of the most recognizable game developers in

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:20.720
the world.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:25.480
And it wasn’t long until they started hosting
tournaments and handing out massive prizes.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:30.019
Despite this roaring start, over the past
few years, Supercell has lost much of the

00:00:30.019 --> 00:00:32.329
momentum that they once had.

00:00:32.329 --> 00:00:35.670
Most of their games have lost the vast majority
of their interest.

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:38.790
And we’re not talking about declines of
40-50%.

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:42.440
We’re talking about declines of over 80%.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:47.000
Clash of Clans, for example, only pulls in
5% of interest that it once used to.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.269
Similarly, Boom Beach only pulls in 4% of
the interest that it once used to.

00:00:51.269 --> 00:00:54.140
A similar story can be seen with Clash Royale
as well.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:59.250
The only major Supercell game that hasn’t
suffered such a decline is Brawl Stars, but

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:03.140
even Brawl Stars is experiencing quite a significant
decline.

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:07.580
On top of this, many of the new games from
Supercell like Rush Wars and Hay Day Pop were

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:10.640
outright shutdown due to concerns regarding
longevity.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:15.460
And as for the games that haven’t been shutdown,
well it’s not much better for them either.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:18.920
Take Supercell’s latest game, Everdale,
for example.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:22.750
The interest in Everdale is so low that you
can’t even see its graph relative to Clash

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:23.750
of Clans.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.940
It’s not just Google trends that’s showing
this trend either.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:29.270
Socialblade paints a very similar picture.

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:32.810
Most of our favorite Clash YouTubers are only
getting a fraction of the views and subscribers

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:33.970
that they once got.

00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:38.980
In the past 3 years, Chief Pat’s subscriber
count has only increased from 2.51 million

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:40.920
to 2.57 million.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:44.630
His viewership isn’t that much better either,
he’s only getting a few hundred thousand

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:46.000
views per month.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.450
Back in his hayday, he would get more views
on each video.

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:55.090
A similar story can be seen with Molt, Galadon,
NickatNyte, ClashWithAsh, and so many more.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:59.590
Now, I’m 100% sure that there’s gonna
be comments down below that claim that Supercell’s

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:02.880
games aren’t dead and that they still have
large player bases.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:08.280
But, honestly most of these players are super
fans or they do it as a job.

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.380
Virtually all of Supercell’s casual base
has ditched their games.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.480
So, while some of their games still have a
decent number of players, there’s no question

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:17.300
that Supercell is not nearly as popular as
they once used to be.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:20.340
So, what happened to Supercell?

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:26.629
PAY TO WIN:
One of the primary factors that made Supercell

00:02:26.629 --> 00:02:30.689
games so popular in the first place was their
unique mode of monetization.

00:02:30.689 --> 00:02:33.189
Supercell didn’t charge users directly to
play the game.

00:02:33.189 --> 00:02:37.489
In fact, you didn’t even have to pay them
a single dime if you didn’t want to.

00:02:37.489 --> 00:02:41.380
Rather, Supercell made all their money from
people who wanted to advance faster.

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:44.659
If you didn’t want to spend years maxing
out your clash of clans base or collecting

00:02:44.659 --> 00:02:48.620
a bunch of clash royale cards, you could spend
money to speed up these processes.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:51.909
This unique revenue stream allowed Supercell
to create quite ambitious games.

00:02:51.909 --> 00:02:56.230
Up until the release of Clash of Clans, virtually
all mobile games were extremely simple and

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:57.230
rudimentary.

00:02:57.230 --> 00:03:01.249
We had games like Temple Run, Fruit Ninja,
and Angry Birds.

00:03:01.249 --> 00:03:05.220
Given the limited revenue from these games,
developers weren’t able to spend that much

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:06.220
on development.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:10.280
But, with Clash of Clans, individual users
were spending hundreds if not thousands of

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:13.980
dollars on the game which allowed Supercell
to splurge on development.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:17.909
This gave casual players an experience that
they couldn’t find anywhere else.

00:03:17.909 --> 00:03:21.939
No free game mobile or otherwise stacked up
to the quality and experience of Clash of

00:03:21.939 --> 00:03:22.939
Clans.

00:03:22.939 --> 00:03:26.950
Aside from being extremely accessible to casual
players, casual players felt like they could

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:29.469
do well in the game without spending any money
on it.

00:03:29.469 --> 00:03:33.870
Sure, they might not become a top player in
the world, but it was realistic for them to

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:35.800
max out their bases within a few years.

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:40.829
With time, however, we saw updates that made
this more and more difficult.

00:03:40.829 --> 00:03:43.590
A perfect example of this is wall upgrades.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:47.500
To max out walls, you had to spend 4 million
gold per wall unit.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:51.109
Only people who played clash of clans know
how big of pain this was.

00:03:51.109 --> 00:03:53.720
For the rest of you, I’ll put it in dollar
terms.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:55.939
To max out your clash of clans base, it cost
$11,000.

00:03:55.939 --> 00:04:01.090
And out of this, nearly $5,000 would go towards
simply maxing out walls.

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:05.270
In other words, nearly half the game was simply
maxing out walls.

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:09.840
I don’t think I need to explain why this
made the game extremely tedious and frustrating

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:12.389
especially for late stage players.

00:04:12.389 --> 00:04:17.280
And honestly, the only reason Supercell made
it so hard to max out walls is because they

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:20.920
knew that the top players were willing to
spend whatever it took to max out their bases.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:24.760
So, this was an easy $5000 from each top player.

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:28.910
While this was extremely profitable for Supercell,
it didn’t take long for players to feel

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.690
that Supercell’s games were becoming pay
to win.

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:34.630
And this become even more evident with Clash
Royale.

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:38.830
Not only did you have to spend insane amounts
of money, but you also had to gamble a bit.

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:42.740
You see, when Clash Royale was launched, you
couldn’t just max out each of your cards

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:44.060
one by one.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:47.520
Instead, you had to buy chests that gave you
a random set of cards.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:51.650
So, if you wanted to max out your account,
you had to keep buying chests until the random

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:54.220
cards happened to be exactly what you need.

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:57.450
And on average, this ended up costing nearly
$30,000.

00:04:57.450 --> 00:05:02.020
Considering this, I don’t think you’d
be surprised to hear that the vast majority

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:07.140
of players never played these games to the
end.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:10.780
DISTRACTIONS:
Aside from it becoming virtually impossible

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:14.790
for casual players to max out their accounts,
we also saw several distractions appear for

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:15.790
these players.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:19.980
While Supercell was one of the first companies
to leverage this freemium business model,

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:22.560
they were by no means the last.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:26.660
Given the insane popularity of Supercell,
basically every game developer became aware

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:30.580
of this alternative mode of monetization,
and it didn’t take long for them to launch

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:32.160
their own offerings.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:37.630
Some of the biggest competitors include Pokemon
Go, PUBG Mobile, and of course Fortnite.

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:42.040
Not only did these games also offer a high
quality experience for free players, but they

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:43.890
were arguably more fair.

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:45.700
Take Fortnite for example.

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:49.540
While you could spend tens of thousands of
dollars collecting every skin in the game,

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:53.370
this would give you absolutely no advantage
when it came to playing the game itself.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:57.720
A pro player could start a new account and
their chances of winning would still be identical.

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:01.660
As these newer games started to gain popularity,
it was only natural that people started leaving

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:02.800
older games.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:06.400
It wasn’t just newer games that were siphoning
Supercell’s user base either.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.680
Another major culprit was social media.

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:12.460
When Clash of Clans came out, mobile social
media was in its infancy.

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:15.740
We were just starting to see apps like Instagram
and Snapchat come out.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:19.510
So, the vast majority of smartphone users
weren’t using their smartphones for social

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:20.510
media.

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:23.440
They primarily used it for productivity or
gaming.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:28.340
But, over time, social media has risen to
become the number 1 use of smartphones.

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:32.140
Many of the largest social media platforms
like Instagram and WhatsApp boast user counts

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:33.940
in the billions.

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:37.880
And as people started flocking over to social
media apps, it just became even harder for

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:40.000
Supercell to hold onto their users.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:44.560
To make things even worse, Supercell wasn’t
just fighting against other mobile apps either.

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:49.510
Over the past 5 years, we’ve seen quite
a surge in pc gaming mostly thanks to AMD.

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:54.090
You see, in 2017, AMD launched a new series
of CPUs called Ryzen.

00:06:54.090 --> 00:06:58.840
And since it’s release, Ryzen has substantially
reduced the cost of PC gaming.

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:03.280
This has prompted more people than ever to
switch over PC gaming, and this trend has

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:07.480
simply been accentuated by the pandemic which
forced people to stay at home.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:10.960
So, in the end, many of the casual gamers
switched over to social media.

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:14.580
Many of the amateurs and enthusiasts switched
over to PC gaming.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:20.650
And as for the remaining mobile gamers, well
they now have more quality options than ever.

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:26.280
CASH OUT:
So far, we’ve primarily discussed factors

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:30.350
that have led to gamers ditching Supercell,
but there’s also an argument to be made

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:34.590
that Supercell has ditched gamers. 10 years
ago, Supercell was a small gaming startup

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:36.440
that was trying to hit it big.

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:40.030
They were hungry to launch the next big game
and make their mark in the industry.

00:07:40.030 --> 00:07:42.710
But, now they’ve already done that.

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:45.410
What’s the motivation to achieve something
even bigger?

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:50.010
Also, we should note that Supercell’s leadership
brilliantly sold the company at the peak of

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:51.010
their popularity.

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:57.540
In June of 2016, Tencent agreed to buy 84%
of the company at an $8.6 billion valuation.

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:01.590
While this was a great financial move for
the company’s leadership and OG employees,

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:04.170
this was likely not a very good move for the
company’s spirit.

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:09.160
You see, Supercell only had a total of 340
employees which means that the buyout was

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:12.010
worth $25 million per employee.

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:15.930
This means that unless you joined months before
the acquisition, you likely received at least

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:17.170
a 6 figure payout.

00:08:17.170 --> 00:08:20.830
Meanwhile, employees that had been around
since the beginning likely received 7 figure

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:23.850
payouts if not multi 7 figure payouts.

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:28.040
In other words, the vast majority of Supercell
employees became well off if not completely

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:29.290
financially free.

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:33.999
While this is an awesome outcome for any startup,
it also drains the company of much of its

00:08:33.999 --> 00:08:34.999
motivation.

00:08:34.999 --> 00:08:36.510
A perfect example of this is Dell.

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:41.459
10 to 15 years ago, Dell was facing a relentless
decline and Michael Dell even came out of

00:08:41.459 --> 00:08:43.400
retirement to save the company.

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:47.240
And one of the biggest issues that he found
was that many of Dell’s employees simply

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:48.240
didn’t care.

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:52.510
They didn’t care about the future of the
company nor did they care about being fired.

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:57.249
You see, Dell stock had minted 2700 millionaires
many of which were decamillionaires.

00:08:57.249 --> 00:09:01.410
In fact, this was so common that people called
them dellionaires.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:06.569
To combat this, Michael had to take Dell private,
layoff significant portions of their workforce,

00:09:06.569 --> 00:09:07.930
and pivot to the server market.

00:09:07.930 --> 00:09:12.709
I don’t know about you, but I don’t think
Supercell is likely to go through such an

00:09:12.709 --> 00:09:13.709
evolution.

00:09:13.709 --> 00:09:17.189
To make things worse, I don’t think their
parent company Tencent cares all that much

00:09:17.189 --> 00:09:18.189
either.

00:09:18.189 --> 00:09:22.920
While $8.6 billion is an insane amount of
money for us peasants, it’s simply a calculated

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:24.350
risk for Tencent.

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:29.749
Tencent has a market cap of over $400 billion
and that’s after crashing over 50%.

00:09:29.749 --> 00:09:34.339
So, I don’t think they’re super motivated
to turn around Supercell either.

00:09:34.339 --> 00:09:38.500
From their perspective, they have stakes in
dozens of gaming companies, and they just

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:41.129
need a few of them to do really well to make
up for such losses.

00:09:41.129 --> 00:09:45.390
So, it’s really up to Supercell alone to
save themselves.

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:52.050
FUTURE OF SUPERCELL:
In the end, Supercell is one of the most iconic

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:54.970
and nostalgic game developers in the world.

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:59.000
Most of us have atleast tried one of their
games if not played them for years.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:03.199
But, in recent history, Supercell hasn’t
been doing all that great.

00:10:03.199 --> 00:10:06.450
Their trend towards pay to win has shunned
away a lot of players.

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:09.930
Not to mention all the extra competition they’ve
been facing from other game developers and

00:10:09.930 --> 00:10:11.180
social media.

00:10:11.180 --> 00:10:14.860
These issues have likely only been worsened
by the buyout which probably softened morale

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:17.360
and spirit amongst employees and executives.

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:20.370
Now, it’s not like Supercell is struggling
to make money.

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:23.120
They’ve introduced several sources of recurring
revenue throughout their games.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:26.670
So, the remaining players are likely quite
profitable.

00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:30.370
But in terms of returning to their former
glory, it’s really just a coinflip.

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:34.199
Supercell’s best bet is to just continue
launching games and hopefully one of them

00:10:34.199 --> 00:10:35.490
will pick up steam.

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:39.769
But, if not, they’ll probably just end up
supporting their most popular games until

00:10:39.769 --> 00:10:44.000
they eventually become unprofitable themselves
at which point they’ll shut these down as

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:45.000
well.

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:48.470
But, fortunately, these games likely still
have several years left before the become

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:53.170
unprofitable, so Supercell has quite a bit
of time to figure something out, but only

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:54.649
time will tell.

00:10:54.649 --> 00:10:56.740
Which Supercell game is your favorite?

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:57.740
Comment that down below.

00:10:57.740 --> 00:11:01.629
Also, drop a like if Supercell games are nostalgic
for you.

